I came out of the main market of the town.
It was two o'clock in the afternoon.
There was a lot of crowd and noise there.
So I decided to go to a quiet place.
I took the water bottle out of my bag.
And I started walking slowly on a hilly path.
There were many turns on the path.
I moved forward at my own pace.
There were some other people on the way too.
A man was walking carrying his heavy bag.
His daughter was with him.
In Mumbai, I am always in a hurry.
But here I was in no hurry.
I looked at the tall trees and the blue sky.
The air was very clean and cool.
There was a lot of peace all around.
After some time, I saw a famous viewpoint.
I stopped there.
I took a deep breath.
This walk was very good for me.
